{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"1|# QG Project Instructions\\n2|\\n3|## Project\\n4|\\n5|```text\\n6|QG\\n7|/home/treshen/Projects/QG/\\n8|```\\n9|\\n10|QG is an existing, in-progress native Ubuntu/Linux video explorer and player.\\n11|Earlier manual Hermes runs may have advanced the implementation farther than the\\n12|control documents indicate. Use actual source, build, tests, and runtime evidence\\n13|when reconciling stale state.\\n14|\\n15|## Source of Truth\\n16|\\n17|Priority:\\n18|\\n19|```text\\n20|1. DESIGN.md\\n21|2. validated actual implementation behavior\\n22|3. DECISIONS.md\\n23|4. dev-guide.md\\n24|5. GUIDE_STATE.md\\n25|6. current task instruction\\n26|```\\n27|\\n28|`DESIGN.md` defines approved product behavior and architecture.\\n29|`dev-guide.md` defines the ordered implementation pipeline.\\n30|`GUIDE_STATE.md` records execution progress.\\n31|`DECISIONS.md` records durable architecture/implementation decisions.\\n32|`REQUIREMENTS_MATRIX.md` records requirement coverage.\\n33|\\n34|## Session Startup\\n35|\\n36|For a development turn:\\n37|\\n38|1. read `GUIDE_STATE.md`;\\n39|2. read relevant `DECISIONS.md`;\\n40|3. read relevant `REQUIREMENTS_MATRIX.md`;\\n41|4. locate the current/next work item in `dev-guide.md`;\\n42|5. read that work item in full;\\n43|6. read only the relevant `DESIGN.md` sections;\\n44|7. inspect the actual implementation/tests/build definitions required by that item.\\n45|\\n46|Use fresh filesystem evidence rather than conversational memory.\\n47|\\n48|## Existing-Project Rule\\n49|\\n50|Treat QG as an existing project.\\n51|Preserve compatible implementation.\\n52|When recorded state and actual implementation disagree, reconcile them using\\n53|source, build, tests, and runtime evidence before advancing.\\n54|\\n55|## Execution Model\\n56|\\n57|Continuous autonomous development is driven by:\\n58|\\n59|```text\\n60|/home/treshen/Projects/QG/hermes/qg-pipeline.py\\n61|```\\n62|\\n6