{"type": "tool_result", "name": "read_file", "output": "{\"content\": \"1238|- Eject/unmount delegates to GIO/UDisks2 asynchronous operations. The action is exposed only when the platform reports that it is supported.\\n1239|\\n1240|### 17.5 Refresh\\n1241|\\n1242|- `QFileSystemWatcher` watches the current directory (and the parent while a re-arm is needed, because watchers are invalidated when a directory is replaced).\\n1243|- Changes debounce 300ms, then a **targeted diff** runs: re-enumerate, compare against the model by identity, and apply minimal `rowsInserted`/`rowsRemoved`/`dataChanged`. This preserves scroll position and avoids the flicker of a full reload.\\n1244|- `F5` forces a full re-enumerate (useful on network filesystems where watchers are unreliable).\\n1245|- A \\\"modified\\\" detection compares `mtime_ns` + `size`; changed files invalidate thumbnails and probe cache for that identity (§18).\\n1246|\\n1247|### 17.6 File operations\\n1248|\\n1249|`FileOperationsService`:\\n1250|\\n1251|- **Rename:** use `renameat2`/`rename` semantics where available, with live collision checks against the current snapshot; extension is preserved by default. The known old→new path mapping is committed with the identity record so application state follows immediately.\\n1252|- **Move / Copy:** use chunked native I/O / `std::filesystem` helpers where safe, with explicit progress, cancellation checkpoints, metadata preservation, and cross-device copy+delete fallback. Operations on GIO-backed locations may delegate to `GFile` APIs so network/GVfs behavior stays desktop-native.\\n1253|- **Reveal in Folder:** call `org.freedesktop.FileManager1.ShowItems` over D-Bus with a file URI; fall back to launching the parent through GIO/`xdg-open`.\\n1254|- **Open With…:** query `GAppInfo` / `GDesktopAppInfo` for the MIME type and launch the chosen application through GIO. QG never maintains its own application registry.\\n1255|- **Properties:** gather `stat`/ownership/permission/MIME information plus QG metadata (favorite/watched/position) into the non-modal QML Properties dialog.\\n1256|\\n1257|All long operations are scheduled off the GUI thread and publish progress/result structs through queued signals. A cancelled operation reports the exact completed subset rather than pretending the entire operation was atomic.\\n1258|\\n1259|### 17.7 Trash\\n1260|\\n1261|`TrashService` implements the freedesktop Trash specification:\\n1262|\\n1263|- Prefer `gio trash <path>` when `gio` is present and the volume supports it (this correctly handles per-volume trash and `.Trash-1000` on removable media).\\n1264|- Fallback: move to `$XDG_DATA_HOME/Trash/files/<name>` with a collision-suffixed name, write a `.trashinfo` file recording the original absolute path and deletion date, per spec.\\n1265|- **Never permanently deletes by default.** Permanent deletion requires `Shift+Delete` and an explicit confirm dialog that names the count and cannot be reached by accident.\\n1266|- Every Trash operation records enough information to **Undo** for the toast window (restore from trash to original path). After the toast expires, recovery is available through the OS trash, and QG links to it where possible.\\n1267|\", \"total_lines\": 1907, \"file_size\": 139848, \"truncated\": true, \"hint\": \"Use offset=1268 to continue reading (showing 1238-1267 of 1907 lines)\", \"is_binary\": false, \"is_image\": false, \"not_found\": false}", "duration_ms": 2, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791452102068}
