tity, and apply minimal `rowsInserted`/`rowsRemoved`/`dataChanged`. This preserves scroll position and avoids the flicker of a full reload.\\n1245:- A \\\"modified\\\" detection compares `mtime_ns` + `size`; changed files invalidate thumbnails and probe cache for that identity (§18).\\n1251:- **Rename:** use `renameat2`/`rename` semantics where available, with live collision checks against the current snapshot; extension is preserved by default. The known old→new path mapping is committed with the identity record so application state follows immediately.\\n1268:### 17.8 Stable file identity\\n1274:- Persisted `paths(path PK, identity)` maps known paths to identities.\\n1276:- **External rename/move** (unknown to QG): on rescan, reconcile by identity — if a new path carries a known inode, the state is adopted; if an identity disappears, its state is retained (not deleted) for a grace period so a reconnect/remount restores it.\\n1277:- **Copy** produces a genuinely new file and therefore new identity/state — correct, since a copy is not the same media.\\n1301:- Cache key is **identity + mtime_ns + size** (and a thumbnailer version), so any change to the source invalidates automatically.\\n1303:- QG's own cache lives under `$XDG_CACHE_HOME/qg/thumbs/` keyed by identity hash; the DB row (`thumbnails`) records identity, source mtime/size, cache path, thumbnailer used, and generation time.\\n1318:Every extraction result carries the token, identity, and the source `(mtime_ns, size)` that were current when it started. Before any model mutation:\\n1339:- Results are cached in SQLite by identity + source mtime/size; a probe is recomputed only when the source changes.\\n1352:- **`PlaybackSession`** is an immutable-value + observable-state object: media identity, path, duration, current position, state (`idle/loading/playing/paused/ended/error`), volume, mute, and the owning surface.\\n1393:- While playing, position is persisted on a **throttled tick (every 5s)** and on pause/stop/close, keyed by identity.\\n1456:- Repositories expose intention-revealing methods (`set_favorite(identity, bool)`, `record_position(identity, ms)`, `remember_recent(path)`), never raw SQL to callers.\\n1470:  identity   TEXT NOT NULL,\\n1477:CREATE INDEX idx_paths_identity ON paths(identity);\\n1479:-- application metadata keyed by identity\\n1481:  identity        TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\n1495:  identity     TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\\n1530:  identity      TEXT NOT NULL,\", \"exit_code\": 0, \"error\": null}", "duration_ms": 83, "is_error": false, "timestamp": 1791452102154}
